const e="What Family Therapy in Brisbane Looks Like Over Christmas | Michelle Barratt Psychology",t="The Christmas period can bring joy, rest, and quality time with family. But for many, it also comes with rising stress, clashing expectations, and emotional t",a='<!--$--><section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75"><li><a class="hover:text-white" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li><a class="hover:text-white active" href="/blog" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Blog</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li class="text-white" aria-current="page">What Family Therapy in Brisbane Looks Like Over Christmas</li></ol></nav><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3">12 December 2025</p><h1 class="text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">What Family Therapy in Brisbane Looks Like Over Christmas</h1><div class="h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="max-w-2xl text-[16px] md:text-[17px] text-white/95 space-y-3"><p>The Christmas period can bring joy, rest, and quality time with family. But for many, it also comes with rising stress, clashing expectations, and emotional tension. In Brisbane, the holiday season lands during the summer heat, when schools</p></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-white text-plum hover:bg-blush " href="/contact">Contact Us</a></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft !py-0"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="py-14 md:py-16"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/pexels-tima-miroshnichenko-5336930.jpg" alt="" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] max-h-[520px] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></div></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">The Christmas period can bring joy, rest, and quality time with family. But for many, it also comes with rising stress, clashing expectations, and emotional tension.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">In Brisbane, the holiday season lands during the summer heat, when schools close, routines disappear, and everyone seems to be either travelling or hosting.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">That mix can stir up a lot more than just cheer. When family dynamics shift and small issues grow bigger under pressure, it’s not surprising that some families feel out of sync. That’s often when we see people asking what kind of help is out there. Family therapy in Brisbane can offer a steady, calm space during a loud and busy season.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It’s not about having all the answers. It’s about creating thoughtful pauses when emotions feel stronger than usual. For many families, just having someone listen without judging allows for softer conversations at a time when tempers might otherwise flare. Even sitting together in a quiet room or sharing a call can feel like a needed reset.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What the Holiday Season Brings for Families</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">The lead-up to Christmas often brings more to worry about than most people expect. There can be pressure to make things perfect, to keep everyone happy, or to juggle stretched schedules without slowing down.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Many parents feel overwhelmed trying to manage work, extended family plans, or end-of-year expectations</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Teenagers may become more withdrawn or short-tempered when routines change, especially with long school breaks and sudden shifts in social contact</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Couples might argue more during this time, especially around money, time spent with in-laws, or how holiday traditions should be handled</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">When daily habits disappear for a few weeks and emotions start bubbling, it’s easy for resentment or frustration to creep in. And while these things often pass, a build-up during the holidays can make home feel less peaceful than it should.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Even small differences, like how to celebrate or who cooks what, can turn into bigger arguments. For some, old wounds can resurface as relatives arrive or new plans collide with familiar traditions. In these moments, having a way to step back and reflect can help keep things from spiralling.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Common Reasons Families Seek Support Over Christmas</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Christmas doesn’t always feel like the “most wonderful time of the year.” Some families reach out because they’re carrying more than they can quietly manage. That doesn’t always mean big problems. Sometimes it’s the same small tension, repeating again and again without resolution.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Common reasons include:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Disagreements about shared parenting time, blended family arrangements, or travel plans</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Grief that feels sharper around Christmas, especially if someone is missing or if the holidays bring reminders of past events</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Miscommunication or silence between family members that builds into bigger emotional disconnects</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It’s often not about fixing everything at once. Families who seek help around this time are usually just looking for steadier ground. Even a bit of outside support can open up new ways to talk through what’s happening and make space for more kindness.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Talking to someone objective can help families spot the habits that can make things harder, and offer small ways to steer conversation in a better direction. For example, learning how to pause before reacting or trying new ways to listen to each other.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">A loss, a major change, or simply a shift in who is present at the Christmas table can affect the mood for everyone. For children and teenagers, changes in routines or missing loved ones might bring feelings that are hard to share with family. Sometimes, having a neutral voice in the room can help all sides understand what’s underneath the anger or sadness.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">How Family Therapy Sessions Work During the Holidays</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">One of the first concerns people have is whether support is even an option during such a packed time of year. Life doesn’t stop over Christmas, so support needs to be adaptable too. The good news is that there are ways to make it work without adding more pressure.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Therapy sessions can be arranged in advance around school holidays, work leave, or family trips</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>In-person appointments in Brisbane may still be available depending on timing, but many people use telehealth for extra flexibility</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>For some, talking from the quiet of their own home helps reduce the emotional load before and after a session</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Michelle Barratt Psychology offers evidence-based family therapy provided by clinical psychologists with experience supporting families, couples, and teens. Sessions can address a wide range of challenges, including anxiety, depression, parenting, communication, and relationship dynamics.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Sometimes just knowing there’s a calm place to land makes the season feel less overwhelming, especially when expectations feel too big or relationships feel stretched. These sessions aren’t about finding someone to blame or pointing out what’s wrong. Instead, the aim is to help everyone feel listened to, and to guide families towards the feeling of being on the same team, even if the issues don’t go away overnight.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Telehealth has become a helpful option, especially recently, because it lets people attend sessions from wherever they feel most comfortable, whether that’s at home, on holiday, or staying with relatives.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">This flexibility can make it much easier for families to keep their support going, even as schedules change. Having a routine check-in each week or fortnight, even for a short session, can provide the touchpoint some families need just to get through a tough period.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Creating Safe Emotional Spaces for Teens and Couples</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Teens and couples are often hit hardest by the tension of Christmas. Teens might not say much, but changes in their mood or energy can signal that they’re struggling. Being around family 24/7 without time for themselves can leave them feeling boxed in. And if they’re already going through challenges, this time of year might just amplify them.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Therapy gives teenagers a space to share how they’re really feeling without worrying they’ll upset someone</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Couples often come in with small problems that were manageable during the year but feel heavier under holiday pressure</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Being able to talk through shared goals or frustrations in a neutral space can help couples feel more connected, not further apart</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Families in Brisbane can access sessions at our Toowong or Wynnum West clinics, or choose the convenience of telehealth which remains available over the holidays. Our psychologists are trained in supportive, practical approaches that make a difference during emotionally intense times.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">During Christmas, when nerves are already frayed, these kinds of emotional check-ins can make a real difference for family connection. By making space for teens to express themselves and for partners to slow down and listen to each other, families can foster a climate of cooperation instead of conflict.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It is often these simple, consistent steps that help the most. For teens, knowing they have somewhere safe to talk, without being told what they should feel, can make it easier to handle big emotions and changes.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Couples benefit too. Checking in with someone who can help guide them through disagreements or old patterns, especially in a warmer and supportive space, can leave them feeling lighter and more in tune, not worn down by the season.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">A Calmer Way Through the Holiday Chaos</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Christmas doesn’t have to be about ticking off lists or keeping everyone smiling. It can be about slowing down, checking in, and making sure everyone feels safe enough to be themselves. When that’s not happening, some families step into therapy not because things feel horrible, but because they want the holidays to feel a little lighter.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Family therapy offers support that doesn’t require a crisis. It just asks all voices to be heard and reminds people they’re not alone. With a little help, it’s possible to move through Christmas with fewer harsh words and more shared understanding, even if the big feelings don’t fully go away. Sometimes, that’s enough.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Making space for one another and finding small ways to reconnect can change the whole mood of the season. Even if everything else stays the same, feeling heard can make a difference that lasts far beyond Christmas.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we believe in easing the holiday stress with support that fosters connection and understanding. Let our family therapy in Brisbane guide you through seasonal challenges with compassion and expertise.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Our experienced team is here to ensure that every family member feels heard and valued, paving the way for a harmonious holiday season. Reach out today to start feeling more connected and at peace this Christmas.</p></div></section><section class="bg-blush "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold mb-8">More articles</h2><div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">23 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising PTSD Counselling Needs in Toowong Adults</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Post-traumatic stress disorder, or PTSD, is not only something that happens to people in movies or in extreme situations. It can grow quietly in everyday lif…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">16 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Online Therapy in Brisbane When You Can’t Find Local Support</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Trying to find a psychologist in Brisbane can feel exhausting. You search, you join waitlists, you juggle your calendar, and still there is no appointment th…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">9 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising Trauma Counselling Needs in Toowong Professionals</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">High-performing professionals in Toowong are often good at holding it together. Work is busy, the pressure is high, and most people tell themselves it is jus…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a></div></div></section><section class="bg-blush"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5">Take the first step</p><h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="mt-5 text-[17px]">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class="mt-3">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class="text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium" href="tel:0731850040">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] " href="/practitioners">Book Online</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac " href="/therapy-services">Explore Services</a></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->',s={title:e,description:t,html:a};export{s as default,t as description,a as html,e as title};
